       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A single 4,250 mg dose is in the range where metformin overdose and lactic acidosis are reported, and 12,750 mg/day has no therapeutic use that I know of. I can't enter an order I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals is the 2,550 mg/day max. I can enter that or another dose you choose.\n- **Add a note to the order** if you want to document your reasoning or titration plan.\n- **Use another route.** If you have an unusual clinical reason for this dose, a clinical pharmacist or the P&T/medication safety process can review it. They can also enter it directly with their own sign-off.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
